Note: Hello Web — Minimal EPL web server
Note: Run with: epl run examples/hello_web/main.epl
Note: Then open http://localhost:8000 in your browser.

Create webapp app

Note: ── Home page (server-rendered HTML) ──
Route "/" shows
    Page "Welcome to EPL"
        Heading "Hello from EPL! 👋"
        Text "This is a web server written entirely in plain English."
        Link "About this app" to "/about"
    End
End

Note: ── About page ──
Route "/about" shows
    Page "About"
        Heading "About Hello Web"
        Text "EPL (English Programming Language) lets you write servers in English."
        Link "Back to home" to "/"
    End
End

Note: ── Health check (JSON API) ──
Route "/api/health" responds with
    Send json Map with status = "ok" and version = "1.0.0" and server = "EPL"
End

Note: ── Time endpoint (JSON API) ──
Route "/api/time" responds with
    Send json Map with time = now() and message = "Server is running"
End

Say "Hello Web running at http://localhost:8000"
Start app on port 8000
